WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Theory of Change
Recap: Theory of Change

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Read each pathway forwards, from inputs to impact, and test every link.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
You explained how your planned work could lead to change, from inputs to long-term impact, and named the assumptions to test with the people affected before and after you launch.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:36.659
2.1 Understanding Theory of Change: A Theory of Change makes your reasoning explicit: if we do this, why might that change follow?

6
00:00:36.659 --> 00:00:46.407
2.2 Defining the problem: The problem is the situation and its causes, not the absence of the solution you have in mind.

7
00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:54.933
2.3 Inputs: Inputs are every resource your activities need, including your own and volunteers’ unpaid time.

8
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:55.933
One lesson at a time

9
00:00:55.933 --> 00:01:04.570
2.4 Activities: Activities are the actions, each starting with a verb, that you and partners take to produce outputs.

10
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:12.837
2.5 Outputs: Outputs show that delivery happened and are mostly within your control, but not that lives improved.

11
00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:22.104
2.6 Outcomes: Outcomes are the changes in people, relationships or conditions between what you deliver and long-term impact.

12
00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:23.104
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:23.104 --> 00:01:31.741
2.7 Long-term impact: Impact is long-term change in lives or conditions that you contribute to alongside many other actors.

14
00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:41.119
2.8 Assumptions, risks and evidence: Before launch almost every link rests on assumptions; the critical ones need evidence and a test.

15
00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:53.719
2.9 Test, write and use your Theory of Change: A Theory of Change is useful when people can read it, question it and use it to decide.

16
00:01:54.319 --> 00:02:05.437
Your pathways shape the structure and people you need in Organise, and become the results framework and indicators you will measure in MEAL.

17
00:02:06.037 --> 00:02:10.837
You check your Theory of Change and download each exercise as a PDF.

18
00:02:12.337 --> 00:02:15.437
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
